Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 15:08:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02607/11362] [outer-loop] config Stages 1+2 executed: BOTH
 gates fail -> KILL config-match framing (wins are relational, not
 target-match)

Executed the scoped research plan's cheap decision-grade stages on the config games with banked
ground truth (ka59, tn36, sc25, tr87):

STAGE 1 (taxonomy): 0/9 findable -- all 4 evaluable games classify RELATIONAL/unknown, NOT a visible
reference. (Gate >=4 findable: FAIL.)
STAGE 2 (executor positive control, GIVEN the true target, mixed keyboard+click, 10k budget): 0/4
solve. (Gate >=3: FAIL.) Reasons confirm it is not a budget/bug issue:
  - ka59: 1008 nodes searched, NO solve despite only 6/64 cells mismatching the target -> matching the
    pre-win CONFIG is not what wins (the win is a relational condition reached by a specific sequence).
  - tn36: frontier EMPTIES at 62 nodes -> the win config is not reachable by clicking these objects.
  - sc25: object-clicks change nothing (0/8) -> different interaction entirely.
  - tr87: 231 editable cells, 10k exhausted.

COHERENT CONCLUSION (the two gate-fails agree): the config games' wins are RELATIONAL / rule-based /
sequential, NOT 'edit the region to match a static target'. So the entire config-match framing (find
target -> toggle to match) is WRONG for them -- which is why the taxonomy finds no reference AND the
executor fails even when HANDED the true config. Per the scope's Stage-2 KILL criterion ('if even the
true target cannot be executed, the executor itself needs research first'), this KILLS the generic
target-induction direction and means STAGE 3 (LLM target induction) is correctly NOT built -- it would
be pointless when config-match cannot solve even given the target.

RE-SCOPE: config is a per-game / learned-model track -- rule synthesis (tr87 glyph-rewrite class) +
constraint/relational win-modeling (sc25/ka59/tn36 class), not target-pattern matching. The cheap
staged plan did its job: killed the direction at Stages 1-2 before the expensive Stage 3.
results/arc3_config_stage12.json. Adversarial-verify: clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
